      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "Under aerobic conditions, LH2 (0.2 g, 1.02 mmol) was dissolved in methanol (10 mL) and YCl3·6H2O (0.15 g, 0.50 mmol) in methanol (10 mL) was added dropwise. The light yellow solution was stirred for 30 min. CuCl2·2H2O (85 mg, 0.50 mmol) in methanol (5 mL) was added in default to avoid [Cu4L4]. Triethylamine (0.2 mL) was added, giving a deep blue solution. After 30 min stirring, the solution was concentrated; any insoluble [Cu4L4] was filtered off. The concentrate was cooled in ice, then triethylamine (0.2 mL) and hexafluoroacetylacetone (0.5 mL) were added, turning the solution clear green. Slow evaporation over 3 days gave green cubic crystals of 2, isolated by filtration and washed with a small amount of methanol (178 mg, 47%). 2 can also be obtained from 4 by adding triethylamine and hexafluoroacetylacetone to a methanolic solution.",
