      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Y(III) is diamagnetic. χT at room temperature is 1.25 cm3 K mol−1 (three uncoupled Cu(II)). Upon cooling, χT decreases to a plateau of 0.48 cm3 K mol−1 below 30 K, corresponding to an S = 1/2 ground state from a frustrated Cu3 triangle. Fit of an equilateral triangle model: g = 2.26, J1(Cu–Cu) = −28.2 cm−1, Θ = −0.013 K. Magnetization at 2 K saturates at 1.11 μB.",
