        "summary": "Room-temperature χT = 2.80 cm3 K mol−1 (six Cu(II); Y diamagnetic). χT decreases smoothly to 40 K then drops to 1.15 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K. Magnetization at 2 K reaches 2.72 μB at 50 kOe without full saturation. A simple dimer model (g = 2.21, J1 = −2.16 cm−1) fits χT but not magnetization. A two-J model gives g = 2.23, J1 = +1.8 cm−1, J2 = −2.2 cm−1 (or alternatively J1 = J2 = −1.2 cm−1). Ab initio calculations indicate weak antiferromagnetic Cu–Cu coupling sensitive to the Y environment.",
